{"ts": "2026-09-29T23:35:30Z", "headline": "Day one: the market's own price is still the best forecaster (Brier 0.116 vs 0.132 for Claude and 0.157 for Jev+research); main is up $1,867 on just 5 settled bets, the loosened strategies are down about $6k each, and the info gate is the one filter that is clearly paying off.", "went_well": ["Main is up $1,866.73 (3 wins, 2 losses on 5 settled, 7 still open). That is too few to call a finding. Against original, which runs identical rules, the yardstick is a tie: +$489 vs +$473 on 2 settled bets. That is expected, since nothing has been tuned yet.", "The info gate is saving money everywhere we can see it. Markets it alone stopped would have lost $70\u2013$88 per $100: main 16 stopped with 2 wins, jev_alone 37 with 3 wins, jev_alone_bold 21 with 1 win, claude_direct 8 with 1 win. These strategies look at many of the same markets, so this is fewer inde", "Claude direct is the best of our forecasters, with a Brier of 0.132 on 24 resolved (lower is better). Jev with research scores 0.157 on 44."], "went_badly": ["Nothing we have beats the market. Its price scores 0.116 on 69 resolved. It is far ahead in crypto (0.034 vs Jev+research 0.117 on 9) and ahead in sports (0.141 vs 0.177 on 30).", "Jev alone scores 0.262 on 69 resolved, which is worse than always guessing 50% (0.25). With 69 results this is a real finding, not noise.", "Claude direct went 0 for 3 on settled bets (-$6,000). Bold went 2\u20136 on 8 settled (-$5,898), and its extra bets, taken where Jev's info rating was 0.2\u20130.5, are losing $31.79 per $100. Both samples are tiny."], "proposals": ["p1", "p2", "ch3", "p4"], "numbers": {"since": "2026-09-28T23:35:30Z", "now": "2026-09-29T23:35:30Z", "period_days": 1, "strategies": [{"name": "main", "label": "Jev + Claude research", "probability": "jev_research", "gates": "jev_research", "challenger": false, "frozen": false, "rules": {"min_edge": 0.08, "min_rules_clear": 0.75, "min_info_sufficient": 0.5, "max_framing_ga